{{Quote|Toughest guy in the galaxy? That would be me.|Humungousaur to the [[Tripledecker]].<ref>''[[The Ultimate Sacrifice]]''</ref>}}
Humungousaur possesses incredible strength, being able to effortlessly lift and throw heavy objects up to a high altitude, even into near-earth orbit.<ref name="Pier Pressure">''[[Pier Pressure]]''</ref><ref name="SD">''[[Special Delivery]]''</ref> Technically speaking, at base size, he is physically stronger than [[Methanosian]]s{{Refn|[[:File:Kevin's Previous Girlfriends.PNG]]|group = DM|name = link}} and [[Crystalsapien (Classic)|Crystalsapien]]s,{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Transformation Duration.PNG]]|group = DM}} but weaker than [[Tetramand (Classic)|Tetramands]],{{Refn|group = DM|name = link}} some [[Highbreed]],<ref name="B10RP2" /><ref name="Grounded">''[[Grounded]]''</ref>{{Refn|[[:File:Highbreed Strength Range.PNG]]|group = DM}} [[Ultimate Vaxasaurian]]s and [[To'kustar (Classic)|To'kustars]]. His tail is also powerful enough to easily knock away [[Malware|Malware's]] third form.<ref name="SP2">''[[Showdown: Part 2]]''</ref>

Similar to [[Four Arms (Classic)|Four Arms]], Humungousaur is strong enough to create shock waves by clapping his hands together.{{Refn|[[:File:Humungousaur Sonic Clap.png]]|group = MW}} Humungousaur can also generate earthquakes.<ref name="AP1">''[[Absolute Power: Part 1]]''</ref>

Humungousaur has the power to increase or decrease his own body size and mass using dimensional displacement.{{Refn|[[:File:How Humungousaur Grows.png]]|group = DM}} He can grow bigger up to nearly 60 feet{{Refn|group = AF Mini Bible|name = bible 4}} at will, increasing his natural strength as he grows.{{Refn|group = DM|name = link}} Humungousaur, at his full-size, is stronger than Tetramands,{{Refn|group = DM|name = link}} but is still weaker than To'kustars.<ref name="IAEF">''[[If All Else Fails]]''</ref> He can also shrink down to about 10 feet.{{Refn|[[:File:Humungousaur Can Shrink.PNG]]|group = DM}} When Humungousaur grows, his dinosaur features become more pronounced, including features such as plates on his back akin to a member of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stegosauria Stegosauria], a crest on the back of his neck, and a thagomizer (set of spikes) on his tail. The plates on his shoulders and arms also separate and grow, giving him a more ferocious look. These features give him an extra edge in battle both defensively and offensively. Humungousaur can also generate his Stegosaurian features without changing size.<ref name="IAEF">''[[If All Else Fails]]''</ref>{{Refn|[[:File:Humungousaur Can Grow Spikes at Normal Size.PNG]]|group = DM}}

Humungousaur possesses a thick, armored hide, which has proven to be durable enough to withstand getting hit by truck,<ref>''[[Prisoner Number 775 is Missing]]''</ref> a fall from a very high altitude,<ref name="B10RP2">''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 2]]''</ref> pass through [[Baz-L]]'s ship's force-field,<ref name="Pier Pressure" /> and survive indirect blasts from an [[Ultimate Vaxasaurian]]'s missiles.<ref name="TFB1">''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]''</ref>

Humungousaur is capable of jumping extremely high despite his size and weight.<ref name="SP2" />

Humungousaur is quite fast and agile for his size, as he could somersault onto one of the [[Forever Knights]]' battle horses,<ref>''[[Eye of the Beholder]]''</ref> perform a slide tackle,<ref name="SD" /> and evade attacks while in mid-air.<ref name="SP2" />

Humungousaur can survive in the vacuum of space for a few minutes.<ref>[[Pierce Wheels]]</ref><ref name="AaB">''[[Above and Beyond]]''</ref>

Humungousaur's immense size and weight make him very useful for moving against strong suction forces<ref>''[[Paradox]]''</ref> and powerful winds.<ref>''[[Ultimate Aggregor (Episode)|Ultimate Aggregor]]''</ref>

Humungousaur has a powerful roar,<ref name="Deep">''[[Deep]]''</ref> which he once used to scare away a large group of reporters.<ref>''[[Fame]]''</ref>

Humungousaur can run on all fours in a similar fashion to a [[Wikipedia:Bull|bull]] or a [[Wikipedia:Rhinoceros|rhinoceros]].<ref>''[[Primus (Episode)|Primus]]''</ref>

