{{Quote|"Might wanna put a little size on."<br>"No room... in here."|Kevin and Humungousaur.<ref name="Grounded"/>}}
Humungousaur with his naturally large physique, makes him a very easy target for enemy attacks. Even his base size makes it impossible for him to fit into small spaces.<ref name="TBS">''[[The Big Story]]''</ref>

Humungousaur is more of a land-based alien, meaning he cannot breathe or swim underwater, though he can hold his breath for a very long time. Furthermore, due to his immense size and weight he can sink in water.<ref name="Deep" />

Being a Vaxasaurian, Humungousaur is at a massive disadvantage against a [[Kaosseffexx Ultimasauria]] due to their ability to trap him in webbing. Furthermore, Humungousaur is unable to lift them without struggling.<ref>''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]''</ref><ref>''[[Stuck on You]]''</ref>

Humungousaur can be stung by an [[Aerophibian (Classic)|Aerophibian]]'s neuroshock blasts.<ref name="GCBC">''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]''</ref>

Humungousaur is vulnerable to acid.<ref>''[[Ghost Town]]''</ref>

Humungousaur is weak against electricity, such as that generated by [[Amperi (Classic)|Amperi]]<ref>''[[Map of Infinity (Episode)|Map of Infinity]]''</ref> and the [[Stalker]].<ref name="VG">''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]''</ref>

Despite being resistant to heat, Humungousaur cannot hold objects, such as sewer lids, if they become too hot for him to hold.<ref name="AD" />

If Humungousaur is under the effects of a cold virus, his strength and stamina will be severely reduced.<ref name="TSoC">''[[The Secret of Chromastone]]''</ref>

==History==
=== Alien Force===
*Humungousaur first appeared in ''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 2]]'', where he battled some [[DNAlien]]s, but was defeated by a [[Highbreed Commander (Ben 10 Returns: Part 2)|Highbreed Commander]]. Then he jumped onto a [[Highbreed Cruiser]] and destroyed its laser cannon before falling off, saving [[Bellwood (Classic)|Bellwood]].
*In ''[[All That Glitters]]'', Humungousaur stopped a highway overpass from collapsing long enough for [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] to save everyone from falling off it.
**The same scene reoccurred on TV during [[Will Harangue]]'s news report in ''[[Fame]]''.
*In ''[[Pier Pressure]]'', Humungousaur saved [[Baz-L]] from an exploding ship.
*In ''[[Max Out]]'', Humungousaur briefly fought a couple of DNAliens.
*In ''[[Be-Knighted]]'', Humungousaur scared [[Squire]] into telling him the truth about the [[Mapmaker]].
** The same scene reoccurred on the slideshow presentation in ''[[Pet Project]]''.
*In ''[[Paradox]]'', Humungousaur saved [[Hugo]] from getting sucked into [[Professor Paradox]]'s [[Chronolauger|time machine]] and changed the present.
*In ''[[Darkstar Rising]]'', Humungousaur defeated a Highbreed before having his powers drained by [[Michael Morningstar (Classic)|Darkstar]]. Later, Humungousaur defeated Darkstar by jumping on him causing Darkstar to be injured.
*In ''[[Good Copy, Bad Copy]]'', Humungousaur appeared thrice. Firstly, [[Albedo|Negative Humungousaur]] battled the [[Forever Knights]] to find about [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s location. Later, Ben as Humungousaur fought Negative [[Jetray (Classic)|Jetray]]. Finally, Negative Humungousaur defeated [[Goop (Classic)|Goop]], but was defeated by [[Swampfire]], forcing the former to switch into Negative [[Big Chill (Classic)|Big Chill]].
*In ''[[Grounded]]'', Humungousaur saved [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] from a Highbreed and was nearly defeated by the latter before [[Carl Tennyson|Carl]] and [[Sandra Tennyson|Sandra]] arrived to save him.
**The same scene reoccurred in a flashback in ''[[The Ultimate Enemy: Part 2]]''.
*In ''[[Unearthed]]'', Humungousaur fought [[Tiny]].
*In ''[[Voided]]'', Humungousaur was defeated by [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|D'Void]], so he switched into [[Brainstorm]].
*In ''[[Inside Man]]'', Humungousaur helped Gwen pull the Oscillator Key, but then had to protect it from a DNAlien ship.
*In ''[[War of the Worlds: Part 2]]'', Humungousaur broke himself, [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]], Gwen, and Kevin out of a prison on [[Augstaka]]. He then confronted the [[Highbreed High Council]] and figured out a way to help them.
*In '''''[[Ben 10: Alien Swarm]]''''', Humungousaur defeated a large swarm of [[Microchip]]s.{{Refn|[[:File:Alien Swarm Chronology.png]]|group = DM}}
*In ''[[Vengeance of Vilgax: Part 2]]'', Humungousaur was defeated by [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]].
*In ''[[Don't Fear the Repo]]'', Humungousaur showed [[Domstol]] the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]]'s ability to transform Ben into aliens.
*In ''[[Simple]]'', Humungousaur ended the debate between the red and blue teams.
*In ''[[Singlehanded]]'', Humungousaur freed himself from [[Sunder]]'s trap, but reverted before they could even fight. Later, Humungousaur battled Sunder before switching into [[Echo Echo]].
*In ''[[If All Else Fails]]'', Humungousaur failed to stop the [[Failsafe]].
*In ''[[Ghost Town]]'', Humungousaur fought an alien in a golf course until Gwen knocked it out with a golfball.
*In ''[[Busy Box]]'', Humungousaur was defeated by the [[Naljian Destructor]].
*In ''[[Primus (Episode)|Primus]]'', [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]] as Humungousaur was defeated by Vilgax.
*In ''[[Above and Beyond]]'', Humungousaur pretended to capture [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]]. Later, Humungousaur fought the [[Plumbers' Helpers]] until they threw him into space.
*In ''[[The Secret of Chromastone]]'', a sick Humungousaur battled Vilgax before switching into Jetray.
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 1]]'', Humungousaur appeared twice. Firstly, Negative Humungousaur revealed the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] to Ben before going [[Ultimate Humungousaur|Ultimate]]. Then, Ben as Humungousaur was defeated by Negative Ultimate Humungousaur and was forced to surrender the Omnitrix to Vilgax.
*In ''[[The Final Battle: Part 2]]'', the Humungousaur [[Bioid]]s defeated Negative Ultimate Humungousaur.

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Fame]]'', Humungousaur scared some reporters away from [[Ben's House|his house]]. He was also seen on TV thrice.
*In ''[[Duped]]'', Sensitive Ben used Humungousaur to defeat two [[Forever Knights]].
*In ''[[Video Games (Episode)|Video Games]]'', Humungousaur was scanned by [[Oliver Thompson]] for the [[Stalker]]. Later, Humungousaur battled the Stalker and figured out how to beat it, so he transformed into [[Nanomech]] to do so.
*In ''[[Too Hot to Handle]]'', Humungousaur fought [[Surgeon]], [[Buzz (Too Hot to Handle)|Buzz]], and [[Hammer]] before going [[Ultimate Humungousaur|Ultimate]].
*In ''[[Hero Time]]'', Humungousaur beat [[Captain Nemesis]] in a train throwing contest. Later, Humungousaur went Ultimate to fight Nemesis.
*In ''[[Ultimate Aggregor (Episode)|Ultimate Aggregor]]'', Humungousaur destroyed [[Aggregor]]'s machine but failed to stop him from absorbing [[Bivalvan|his]] [[Galapagus|five]] [[Andreas|alien]] [[Ra'ad|prisoners]] [[P'Andor|and]] becoming [[Ultimate Aggregor]].
*In ''[[Map of Infinity (Episode)|Map of Infinity]]'', Humungousaur furiously battled Ultimate Aggregor in [[Los Soledad]] but was defeated.
*In ''[[Deep]]'', Humungousaur, while drowning, scared away some fish aliens before he switched into [[Ampfibian (Classic)|Ampfibian]].
*In ''[[Where the Magic Happens]]'', Humungousaur battled [[Addwaitya's Pallorfang]] and was crystallized by [[Addwaitya]], so he went Ultimate.
*In ''[[Perplexahedron (Episode)|Perplexahedron]]'', Humungousaur avoided some lasers on the [[Perplexahedron]] and defeated one of the [[Techno Guard]]s.
*In ''[[...Nor Iron Bars a Cage]]'', Humungousaur defeated two of [[Morgg]]'s robot guards and accidentally inhaled some alien dream dust which made him attack [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]], who he thought was a [[Havoc Beast]].
*In ''[[The Enemy of My Enemy]]'', Humungousaur went Ultimate to fight [[Ultimate Kevin]].
*In ''[[Absolute Power: Part 1]]'', Humungousaur beat up [[Vulkanus]] to find out about Ultimate Kevin's location.
*In ''[[Eye of the Beholder]]'', Humungousaur defeated some Forever Knights.
*In ''[[The Big Story]]'', a [[Plant Clone Ben|Plant Clone of Ben]] as Humungousaur failed to capture [[Jimmy Jones|Jimmy]] before switching into [[Cannonbolt (Classic)|Cannonbolt]] offscreen.
*In ''[[Girl Trouble]]'', Humungousaur fought [[Antonio]] before going Ultimate. Humungousaur appeared again later when he was changing back to Ben.
*In ''[[Revenge of the Swarm]]'', a tiny Humungousaur was defeated by a clone of [[Dr. Victor Valadis]] in a dream.
*In ''[[The Creature From Beyond]]'', Humungousaur disarmed [[Sir Cyrus]] so that they could talk.
*In ''[[It's Not Easy Being Gwen]]'', Humungousaur battled [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo's]] [[Mutant Frog|mutant frogs]].
*In ''[[Prisoner Number 775 is Missing]]'', Humungousaur fought [[Prisoner 775]].
*In ''[[The Ultimate Sacrifice]]'', Humungousaur battled the [[Tripledecker]] before going Ultimate.
*In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]'', Humungousaur came out of the inter-dimensional rift and fought [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]] before switching into [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]].
*In ''[[Solitary Alignment]]'', Humungousaur fought [[Sir George]], who used the [[Ascalon]] to revert him to [[Human (Classic)|human]]. Later, Humungousaur went Ultimate to battle Sir George again. Humungousaur was seen again when he was changing back to Ben.
*In ''[[Inspector 13]]'', Gwen as Humungousaur prepared to break into the [[Techadon Factory]] before being switched into [[Upchuck|Murk Upchuck]].
*In ''[[Catch a Falling Star]]'', Humungousaur was used to impress [[Maureen Nocturne|Ms. Nocturne]] so Gwen could get information from her.
*In ''[[Couples Retreat]]'', Humungousaur was overpowered by [[Michael Morningstar (Classic)|Michael Morningstar]], so he went Ultimate. Humungousaur appeared again later when he was changing back to Ben.
*In ''[[The Eggman Cometh]]'', Humungousaur broke into Dr. Animo's barn.
*In ''[[The Ultimate Enemy: Part 1]]'', Humungousaur battled [[Ultimate Vilgax]] with Sir George and was defeated by a [[Dagon|possessed]] Gwen.

